 "notes": "Louisiana 5th and 6th go to a 12 December 2026 runoff (WAFB): LA-5 Democrat Pat Moore vs Republican Gabe Firment; LA-6 Democrat Chauna Banks vs Republican Blake Miguez (Republican Rick Edmonds missed the runoff by 972 votes, so that second spot could shift with late counts or a recount). Missouri used its 2022 map for the general because the Supreme Court halted the 2025 map (KCTV5, St. Louis Public Radio); district numbers are unchanged. Arkansas 2nd was close (Hill about 50.9% to 49.1%, about 4,400 votes); AP called it for Hill, but the Jones campaign urged counting every vote and I saw no concession. Oklahoma 5th: Bice listed at 49.49% (plurality; no runoff in Oklahoma general). Kansas 1st and 4th rest on a Kansas Reflector article seen only through a search summary (page not opened directly), which says all four Kansas incumbents held their seats (Mann beat Lauren Reinhold, Estes beat Katy Tyndell). Several vote shares are election-night figures, not certified. Missouri Independent and Arkansas Advocate pages returned 403 and were not opened; other sources used instead."
}
